If you have ansi loaded [device=c:\dos\ansi.sys or equivalent located in your
config.sys file (moot point, nethack wouldn't work very well without it :)], use 
the following files replacing <Esc> with char 27:

remap.bat
rem <Esc>[0;120;81p
rem <Esc>[81;0;120p
<Ctrl-Z>

remap1.bat
rem <Esc>[0;120;0;120p
rem <Esc>[81;81p
<Ctrl-Z>

These two files will remap your keyboard placing 'Q' at the <Alt-1> location
and <Alt-1> at the 'Q' location. 

Type remap.bat before entering nethack and remap1.bat after exiting.

0;120 is the ansi code for <Alt-1> and 81 is the ansi code for 'Q'.

Then you wouldn't have to recompile nethack.

